# Flashback (2011-2012). The largest Mac infection of its time: a fake Flash installer, later a silent Java exploit.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee organises a team offsite on a Mac, orders lunch safely, then meets Flashback on a recipe site.
# The victim is invented: Flashback hit ordinary Mac users on ordinary websites, not one profession.
os macos
user Dana Okafor
about
  | Flashback first posed as a Flash Player installer that asked for the Mac's admin password. In 2012 it used an unpatched Java flaw on hacked websites, so visiting a page was enough.
  | More than 600,000 Macs ran it. It hid in the browsers and rerouted clicks on search results through advertisers, who paid for each one. Dana's office job is invented: the real victims were ordinary Mac users.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, office coordinator at Northwind Traders, working on your {PC|Mac}. On Friday the team has its offsite, and you are booking everything for it.
  | It is mid-morning. You have finished 3 of today's 5 offsite jobs. Two to go: lunch, then a dessert for the bake-off.
  | The logins you need are in text files on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 3 5 Offsite jobs done today

# Dana's desk: the details she copies from (soft flag: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/harbor-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Harbor Kitchen team orders
  | Email: dana.okafor@northwind.example
  | Password: Lunch-2026!

