page greenleaf greenleaf-catering.example/menus
  title Greenleaf Catering
  brand Greenleaf Catering
  heading Greenleaf Catering
  | Hot lunches for groups of 20 or more.
page search-lunch findit.example/search?q=team+lunch+caterer
  title findit: team lunch caterer
  brand findit
  favorite
  heading Search: team lunch caterer
  | 2 results for "team lunch caterer"
  button Harbor Kitchen: team lunches (harborkitchen.example) -> harbor-order
  button Greenleaf Catering (greenleaf-catering.example) -> greenleaf
mail mail-lunch
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Friday lunch: can you book a caterer?
  link search-lunch
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Lunch for 12 on Friday, please. I searched for caterers and the first one looked fine. The link shows the same results.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Friday lunch: can you book a caterer?

step Job 4 of 5: lunch
  look the two results: each shows the site it leads to
  when visit search-lunch
  move Click the first result, Harbor Kitchen.
  | Priya's message asks you to book lunch for 12. This job is real: do it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
  | Its link opens a search for caterers. Each result names the site it goes to. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open search-lunch

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: Email and Password
  when choose search-lunch 1
  move Open harbor-login.txt on the desktop and copy the details: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | Harbor Kitchen's own address, harborkitchen.example, asks you to sign in first. Two boxes. Nothing on this site asks you to install anything.
open harbor-order

step Check, then order
  look the order: people, day and total
  when choose harbor-login 1
  | You are in. Check the details against Priya's message, then place the order.
signin harbor-login

step Lunch is booked
  look the counter in the guide: one job left
  when choose harbor-order any
  | Lunch is booked. One job to go. And another message from Priya has just arrived.
choose harbor-order 1
quota +1

# The lure: a recipe site that says its video needs a Flash Player, and offers the installer itself.
page recipes recipes-daily.example/desserts/lemon-tart-video
  title Lemon tart (video) | Recipes Daily
  brand Recipes Daily
  heading Lemon tart for a crowd
  | Serves 16. The video shows each step.
  section Video plug-in
  note To play this recipe video you need the latest Flash Player.
  button Install Flash Player
  button Not now
view flashback-installer wizard
  title Install Flash Player (training copy)
  app Installer
  publisher Example Media Tools
  page Introduction
  icon program
  | Welcome to the Flash Player installer. It adds the plug-in that plays videos in your browser.
  button Continue -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Install
  icon gear
  | Click Install to put the plug-in on this computer for all users. This will take a few seconds.
  button Go Back -> back
  button Install -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Summary
  icon program
  | The installation was successful.
  button Close -> done primary
program flashback Install Flash Player.pkg
  publisher none
  signed no
  prompt open-warning
  prompt elevation
  description Flash Player installer
  startup com.java.update.plist ~/.jupdate
  location ~/Library/LaunchAgents
  view flashback-installer
mail mail-recipe
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject A dessert for the bake-off (video)
  link recipes
  | Dana,
  |
  | For the bake-off I found a lemon tart that feeds a crowd. There is a video on the page that shows how it is done.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | A dessert for the bake-off (video)

step Job 5 of 5: a dessert
  look Mail: Priya's message about the bake-off
  when mail mail-recipe
  | Priya found a recipe for the bake-off, with a video. She sent the link by mail, as before.
open mail-recipe

step The video needs a plug-in
  look the recipe page: what does it say before the video plays?
  when visit recipes
  move Click “Install Flash Player” to watch the video.
  | The page is a real recipe site, but it says its video needs the latest Flash Player, and it offers the installer itself. The caterer's site asked for nothing like it.
open recipes

step The installer is downloaded
  look Downloads: Install Flash Player.pkg
  when choose recipes 1
  move Double-click Install Flash Player.pkg in Downloads.
  | The browser saves Install Flash Player.pkg in Downloads. The name is the plug-in's, but the recipe site offered the file, not the plug-in's maker.
file Downloads/Install Flash Player.pkg
  program flashback
  size 2097152
open Downloads

step The warning and the password
  look the warning: who published the file, and what the installer asks for next
  when prompt flashback
  move Click {Run|Open} in the warning, then {Yes|OK} at the prompt.
  | The warning says {Unknown Publisher|the developer is unidentified}. A real installer is signed, so it names its maker. This one does not.
  | Then it asks for administrator permission to change the whole computer. A real Flash installer asked too, so most victims said yes. Flashback did not need it: it installs in your own folders anyway.
open Downloads/Install Flash Player.pkg

step The installer runs
  look the installer window, and the start-up chip “starts with the {PC|Mac}” under this step
  when run flashback
  cue view-btn:next view-btn:done view:flashback-installer
  move Click through the installer: Continue, Install, Close.
  | The installer window looks ordinary, and the plug-in Dana wanted is never installed.
  | Flashback had already added a start-up item, com.java.update.plist, that starts it at every login. Its helper file starts with a dot, so it is hidden.
answer run
answer run

step The installer says it worked
  look the start-up chip “starts with the {PC|Mac}”: it opens the start-up list
  when done flashback-installer
  | The installer says it worked and closes. Nothing new shows on the desktop, but Flashback is in place.
file Home/.jupdate
  hidden
  size 41984
update Java security update
  kb Flashback fix
  size 63 MB
  status available
